From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: Fix the RX_TH threshold encoding

The EMAC RX_CTL1 RX_TH field (bits 5:4) encodes 00 = 64 bytes and
01 = 32 bytes (H616 user manual v1.0, 6.5.10; 10 = 96, 11 = 128 as in
the driver). The driver has the first two swapped. The values are only
used in RX threshold mode, which dwmac-sun8i never selects while RX
checksum offload is on, so no current configuration is affected.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -201,8 +201,9 @@
 /* Used in RX_CTL1*/
 #define EMAC_RX_MD              BIT(1)
 #define EMAC_RX_TH_MASK		GENMASK(5, 4)
-#define EMAC_RX_TH_32		0
-#define EMAC_RX_TH_64		(0x1 << 4)
+/* RX_CTL1 RX_TH encoding (H616 UM 6.5.10): 00 = 64, 01 = 32 bytes */
+#define EMAC_RX_TH_32		(0x1 << 4)
+#define EMAC_RX_TH_64		0
 #define EMAC_RX_TH_96		(0x2 << 4)
 #define EMAC_RX_TH_128		(0x3 << 4)
 #define EMAC_RX_DMA_EN  BIT(30)
